    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I implemented to reject creating an owner with a duplicate (case-insensitive) email and respond 409:\n\n**New files**\n- `CheckOwnerEmailUnique.java` \u2014 a pipeline step that, after `ValidateOwner` has lower-cased the email, compares it against every existing owner's email (also lower-cased) and throws `OwnerEmailDuplicateException` on a match. Email is optional, so a null email is left alone.\n- `OwnerEmailDuplicateException.java` \u2014 a checked exception (`extends Exception`) mirroring the telephone-duplicate pattern.\n- `OwnerEmailDuplicateExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`.\n- `...OwnerEmailDuplicateException.yml` \u2014 escalation wiring for the handler.\n\n**Edited**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `checkEmail` step (governed by `transaction`) between `checkTelephone` and `checkHousehold`.\n\nThis follows the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (one public method per class, `@Val` to read the republished body, duplicate detection via the repository, 409 through an escalation handler). The `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` case and the full suite pass.",
