        "cost_usd": 0.23474499999999998,
        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a faithful, additive mirror of the existing `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique` feature, which is clearly the established pattern in this codebase for \"reject-on-duplicate-field-with-409\" at owner creation.\n\n- **Logic in the right unit.** The uniqueness check is its own function class (`CheckOwnerEmailUnique`), wired as its own pipeline step \u2014 exactly matching the sibling `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique`, not bolted into `ValidateOwner` or `BuildOwner`. The `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` + `OwnerRepository` signature and the `service` method name match the sibling precisely.\n- **Error handling idiomatic.** Checked `OwnerEmailDuplicateException` + `OwnerEmailDuplicateExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML follow the per-exception handler convention in AGENTS.md and are structurally identical to the telephone duplicate trio (same 409 `{\"errors\":[\"...\"]}` body shape).\n- **No duplication beyond the deliberate parallel structure.** The near-identical shape to the telephone feature is the codebase's intended symmetry, not accidental copy-paste that should be abstracted \u2014 there's no shared-helper precedent here, and inventing one for two call sites would be less natural than the existing convention.\n- **Pipeline wiring is coherent.** `checkTelephone \u2192 checkEmail \u2192 checkHousehold`, each with `govern: [ transaction ]`, slots in cleanly and keeps governance consistent across the write pipeline.\n- **The optional-email null guard** is consistent with `ValidateOwner`'s treatment of email as optional, and the dependency on `ValidateOwner` having lower-cased the request email is documented in the class Javadoc, mirroring how the telephone class documents its E.164 dependency.\n\nNothing is becoming a catch-all; a maintainer of this repo would find this the natural way to add the feature."
      }
